  {
   "mark": "spring_in",
   "id": "spring_view",
   "say": "The spring comes up in a stone-lined basin in the middle of the town, cold enough to hurt the teeth. The fence round it is hung with things: little wooden legs and hands and eyes, a tin brooch, a twist of somebody's hair. The town walks round the fence, not through it, and lowers its voice going past."
  }
